            <ArticleTitle>Red clover (Trifolium pratense) monograph: a clinical decision support tool.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>49-72</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Red clover, a legume resembling soy is used by man as a phytoestrogen. Other uses include asthma, pertussis, cancer and gout. The authors systematically review this herb in terms of pharmacology, efficacy, safety, side effects, standardization, dosing, toxicology as well as other parameters.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
